    "title": "Baldwin Co. food pantry dips into Christmas supplies to cover surge in Thanksgiving demand - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Andrea Ramey ,\n1 days ago SPANISH FORT, Ala. (NBC 15) — Prodisee Pantry prepared for an additional 100 families for the food distribution event on Tuesday. Executive Director Deann Servos says last year at this event they served 250 families and were expecting 350 this year. In addition to groceries, the Spanish Fort food pantry also handed out Thanksgiving meals. Servos says this is the first time in 23 years they had to borrow from their own Christmas supplies to cover the Thanksgiving demand. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak 4",
